{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas","id":1551559,"title":"Lineage Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-10T07:55:11-07:00","id":1551559,"title":"Lineage Ideas","content":"I've had a few inspirations for lineages and extempore kicking around for a while now. I'm not really planning on doing anything with them, but here's how I might approach them if I did. Any thoughts or suggestions are appreciated.<br /> <br /> These first two are from ideas that pop up in fiction with some frequency:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:#323e4f\">The GELF \u2013 Genetically Engineered Lifeforms</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Inspirations \u2013 Neosapiens (Exosquad), Apes (Planet of the Apes), Eve (Parasite Eve)</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Of those inspirations, the Neosapiens from the critically underrated Exosquad are by far the biggest influence. They work particularly well as Prometheans because of their place in their story and particular traits that mesh well with the Promethean condition and set them apart from humanity.<br /> <br /> The Neos are a workforce of genetically engineered humans designed to be able to handle the harsh climates of other planets. They are quite intelligent but lack creativity and tend towards rigid thinking. They also can develop a degenerative disease that causes them to dissolve slowly into liquid. This doesn\u2019t fit Prometheans, per se, but it does suggest the way that they make more of themselves.<br /> <br /> The Neo-mitochondrial creatures from Parasite Eve, though, work particularly well as GELF pandorans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Humour \u2013 Cytoplasm or Lymph</span></b><br /> <br /> This takes its name from the intra- or intercellular fluids. The imbalance of the GELF tends towards a lack of creativity and reflection. This manifests as an unwillingness to change course once they\u2019ve started a path, to fall back on older patterns when they struggle, and in extreme cases to revert to primal behaviors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Torment \u2013 Rigidity and Regression</span></b><br /> <br /> When in the grips of Torment the GELF find themselves unable to adapt. They double down on whatever they are currently doing, especially if it isn\u2019t working. If and when that fails completely they will fall towards atavistic behaviors, though whether that is their own older patterns, primal and bestial behaviors, or habits of the people they were created from varies from GELF to GELF.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Disquiet - Narrowly Defined Roles</span></b><br /> <br /> People tend to compartmentalize the GELF into narrowly defined categories. They act predictably as long as the Promethean conforms to that role, but the roles are so narrowly defined that\u2019s almost never possible forever. Even when humans treat them as allies it is less \u2018friends\u2019 and more as \u2018tokens\u2019 or as \u2018domesticated.\u2019 When the GELF do show unexpected opinions or wants, people are quick to recompartmentalize them in negative ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Wasteland</span></b><br /> <br /> GELF wastelands tend to cause miasma and unhealth, most commonly in the form of mutations, growths, and in extreme cases malignancies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Potential Generation</span></b><br /> <br /> The GELF are not constructed, they are grown from appropriate sources. Like some other Lineages they most frequently use human remains, but it is not parts that they need, it is biomass.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Potential Bestowments</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\"><i>Clone Body </i></span></b><br /> <br /> The GELF might have the ability to reincarnate by transferring themselves to other sources of biomass.</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This one centers more around the motivation for creating the lineage in the first place. One recurring reason that the Mad Scientist toils in his lab is to create the ULTIMATE LIFEFORM! Mwa ha ha!<br /> <br /> Quite why they want this or why they think they are any judge of what counts as perfection or supremacy is anyone\u2019s guess, but it is a motivation that I don\u2019t see in any of the current lineages.<br /> <br /> This is great source material for a Lineage, but probably not one that takes to the Pilgrimage well. Ultimate Life Forms in fiction tend to consider themselves superior to humanity and don\u2019t see the need to change into something lesser. The other main issue with using them as inspiration is they are very diverse. Their Torments vary wildly, though they are often blinded by their arrogance, and they could easily fit with many of the extant Humours. As such, each of the inspirations is more likely a member of a different lineage than a variant of the same core one.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There isn\u2019t a clear example that fits more with Promethean than the rest, though Adam might make the most sense in a CofD setting. I\u2019m not familiar enough with that season of Buffy to use him as a template, though.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:#323e4f\">The Ultimate Life Forms</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">I<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">nspirations \u2013 Cell (DBZ), Adam (Buffy), Daleks (Doctor Who), Doomsday (Superman)</span></span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Humour \u2013 Any (or Ichor)</span></b><br /> <br /> Ultimate Life Forms could use any of the existing Humours, though Yellow Bile and Phlegm fit particularly well. If they do have a unique humour, I would suggest the name Ichor, the blood of the gods.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Torment \u2013 Arrogance and Blindness</span></b><br /> <br /> While their Torment will be heavily flavored by their Humour, it should also carry a distinct element of pride. They don\u2019t do well when their superiority is called into question and they don\u2019t like subservience, which makes sense as in many of their stories they kill their creators.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Disquiet - Hatred</span></b><br /> <br /> Most likely out and out hatred. Ultimate Life Form inspirations tend to be monsters anyways, here they will be seen as such whether their personality matches or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Wasteland - Mutual Animosity</span></b><br /> <br /> In ULF wastelands, people just do not get along and do not trust in other people\u2019s humanity. Competition and hoarding become common as things run down as if they were never maintained.<br /> \u200b</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T05:03:35-07:00","id":1551586,"title":"","content":"I always thought that it was a mistake to make an Unfleshed Lineage, and that &quot;Unfleshed&quot; should have been implemented in 2e more like how it was in 1e: as a sort of &quot;overlay&quot; to the Promethean, a high-tech version of the Construct. Because it's not really about the Promethean's personality or powers so much as it's about what it's made of. <br /> <br /> But 2e <i>did</i> make it a Lineage; and it did so by shaving off the &quot;made to serve a purpose&quot; part of the Tammuz and expanding it to a full Lineage. This leads to the oddity of having five Lineages that are normally made out of flesh and blood but <i>can</i> be made out of inert materials instead, and one Lineage that must be made out of inert materials. Were I to run a 2e <b>Promethean</b> game, I would either ditch the Unfleshed Lineage, or I would keep it but allow for &quot;fleshy&quot; Unfleshed as well as the more common Unfleshed that's made out of inert materials. <br /> <br /> An example of a &quot;fleshy&quot; Unfleshed would be a genetically engineered lifeform. <br /> <br /> You might also look more into Clones. <br /> <br /> As for the Ultimate Lifeform, I'd be more inclined to handle that as a Refinement. In particular, I could see it as the Refinement of Argent (the &quot;crossover Refinement&quot;) but with a focus on Deviants (the monsters who were created through an effort to improve on ordinary humanity). <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Though speaking of Deviants, bear in mind that one of the Origins for a Deviant is the Genotypal \u2014 the ones who were Born that way. This can be used for &quot;Remade&quot; who were never human, or even organic, to begin with: for example, androids or aliens. If your Ultimate Lifeform isn't pursuing a Pilgrimage, it might actually be a Genotypal Deviant rather than a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T07:22:50-07:00","id":1551588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551586#post1551586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought that it was a mistake to make an Unfleshed Lineage, and that &quot;Unfleshed&quot; should have been implemented in 2e more like how it was in 1e: as a sort of &quot;overlay&quot; to the Promethean, a high-tech version of the Construct. Because it's not really about the Promethean's personality or powers so much as it's about what it's made of.<br /> <br /> But 2e <i>did</i> make it a Lineage; and it did so by shaving off the &quot;made to serve a purpose&quot; part of the Tammuz and expanding it to a full Lineage. This leads to the oddity of having five Lineages that are normally made out of flesh and blood but <i>can</i> be made out of inert materials instead, and one Lineage that must be made out of inert materials. Were I to run a 2e <b>Promethean</b> game, I would either ditch the Unfleshed Lineage, or I would keep it but allow for &quot;fleshy&quot; Unfleshed as well as the more common Unfleshed that's made out of inert materials.<br /> <br /> An example of a &quot;fleshy&quot; Unfleshed would be a genetically engineered lifeform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly I can see the grown from biomass being a legitimate way the Unfleshed could make a fleshy Unfleshed. The result wouldn't really be the same as what I see in the GELF. The closest they come is that they were both created for tasks, but the GELF respond to that very differently than the Unfleshed or Tammuz. The GELF are centered more around the tension of being forced into a second class servant role when they don't fit the role. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You might also look more into Clones. </div> </div> </div>There is a cloning aspect to the Neos, but I overall think they don't fit the Promethean version of clones. They are complete, or at least incompletely complete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Ultimate Lifeform, I'd be more inclined to handle that as a Refinement. In particular, I could see it as the Refinement of Argent (the &quot;crossover Refinement&quot;) but with a focus on Deviants (the monsters who were created through an effort to improve on ordinary humanity).<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Though speaking of Deviants, bear in mind that one of the Origins for a Deviant is the Genotypal \u2014 the ones who were Born that way. This can be used for &quot;Remade&quot; who were never human, or even organic, to begin with: for example, androids or aliens. If your Ultimate Lifeform isn't pursuing a Pilgrimage, it might actually be a Genotypal Deviant rather than a Promethean. </div> </div> </div>The one part of ULFs that really resonates with Promethean is their created nature, and specifically that common motivation in their Demiurge. Apart from that, they don't fit many of the themes of the line. Or, they do, but in the cautionary sense.<br /> <br /> Because the core idea is tied into the reason for their creation, I don't think a Refinement really captures them. On the flip side, you are right that Deviant may be the best fit, though I haven't read much of it. How well do they fit with the themes of that line?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T08:12:11-07:00","id":1551589,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For this one, the idea of the Lineage came before finding an example. Prometheans can be created for many reasons, and childish fantasies and fears are surprisingly powerful. It wouldn\u2019t be unreasonable for a child to accidentally create a Promethean to protect themselves against the dark, or to be a friend, or any number of reasons.<br /> <br /> This would be a Lineage that starts from (and can probably masquerade as) children\u2019s toys and that has elements that push it to stay connected to that role. And there are plenty of stories of mistrusted toys to choose from. There are also a number of stories of toys that want to be more than toys.<br /> <br /> I would stress that Pinocchio is not a good example of this lineage, the best iconic source is instead The Velveteen Rabbit. That story also happens to offer a great name for the Lineage.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:#323e4f\">Skin Horses \u2013 The Creations of Children</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Inspirations \u2013 The Velveteen Rabbit, Hobbes, Talking Tina (The Twilight Zone)</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Humour - Blood</span></b><br /> <br /> Really, they could have a number of humours but I think that passion of Blood turned towards a nurturing or protective role fits best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Torment \u2013 Dependency</span></b><br /> <br /> Skin Horses have a deep need to foster, most often children, and in the depths of torment that can turn towards infantilizing or objectifying or possessing that person. On the flip side separation from their charges induces obsession and depression, punctuated by rage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Disquiet - Unhealth</span></b><br /> <br /> Sooner or later people will become concerned about the safety of the toy. It will be seen as mentally unhealthy, infectious, or unsafe. When the Skin Horse manifests as a person rather than a toy, that person will be an unhealthy influence, or possibly as a poor soul that needs help, preferably help that comes far away from here. Whatever the case, they are not safe to keep around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Wasteland - Askew</span></b><br /> <br /> The Skin Horse wasteland reinforces their Disquiet. It spreads malaise, and while it doesn\u2019t actually give people mental conditions it does play with lighting and sound to make senses unreliable in a way that puts people off balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Potential Bestowments</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\"><i>A Child\u2019s Plaything</i></span></b><br /> <br /> The Skin Horse can appear to be a completely normal child\u2019s toy.<br /> </span><br /> <hr /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T11:33:58-07:00","id":1551593,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, the GELF and ULF don't conceptually feel like Prometheans for the simple reason that the Created are Artificial Life in a more involved sense than being made of lab-grown tissue \u2014 Prometheans don't grow up and age for reasons that have no scientific biological explanation and little active occult explanation (contrast with Kindred vampires, who are magically restored to the state of their Embrace each night), and there's a reason failed Prometheans turn into inanimate objects instead of corpse parts when inactive. As mentioned, Genotypal deviants are much more in line with the tropes of &quot;vat-grown workforce&quot; or &quot;attempted evolutionary pinnacle.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T14:11:24-07:00","id":1551596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551593#post1551593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, the GELF and ULF don't conceptually feel like Prometheans for the simple reason that the Created are Artificial Life in a more involved sense than being made of lab-grown tissue \u2014 Prometheans don't grow up and age for reasons that have no scientific biological explanation and little active occult explanation (contrast with Kindred vampires, who are magically restored to the state of their Embrace each night), and there's a reason failed Prometheans turn into inanimate objects instead of corpse parts when inactive. As mentioned, Genotypal deviants are much more in line with the tropes of &quot;vat-grown workforce&quot; or &quot;attempted evolutionary pinnacle.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you treat them as a strictly scientifically grown workforce then, no they don't fit, but that's not the idea. The Neosapiens are an inspiration for their themes and role in their story, not because they map to promethean alchemy. The GELF are supposed to be what would happen if a Demiurge tried to make something like that, but ended up with a Promethean instead. Like the other lineages they take their inspiration and reinterpret it through the lens of Pyros. If that is reasonable for robots and clones, it is reasonable for genetically engineered life forms.<br /> <br /> If it helps, I actually imagine that for the GELF, the process of growing from biomass is less devouring and growing new flesh and more breaking the original flesh down to cells and rebuilding a body from those cells. That seems the right fit for me. The Neos may be the big inspiration for their torment, disquiet, and the rest, but their &quot;biology&quot; has more to do with Parasite Eve.<br /> <br /> For the ULF, there is no assumption about how they are made, and while three of the four inspirations are lab grown, one of them is literally fused together from various monstrous parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T15:06:40-07:00","id":1551597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551589#post1551589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For this one, the idea of the Lineage came before finding an example. Prometheans can be created for many reasons, and childish fantasies and fears are surprisingly powerful. It wouldn\u2019t be unreasonable for a child to accidentally create a Promethean to protect themselves against the dark, or to be a friend, or any number of reasons.<br /> <br /> This would be a Lineage that starts from (and can probably masquerade as) children\u2019s toys and that has elements that push it to stay connected to that role. And there are plenty of stories of mistrusted toys to choose from. There are also a number of stories of toys that want to be more than toys.<br /> <br /> I would stress that Pinocchio is not a good example of this lineage, the best iconic source is instead The Velveteen Rabbit. That story also happens to offer a great name for the Lineage.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:#323e4f\">Skin Horses \u2013 The Creations of Children</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri Light\"><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Inspirations \u2013 The Velveteen Rabbit, Hobbes, Talking Tina (The Twilight Zone)</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Humour - Blood</span></b><br /> <br /> Really, they could have a number of humours but I think that passion of Blood turned towards a nurturing or protective role fits best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Torment \u2013 Dependency</span></b><br /> <br /> Skin Horses have a deep need to foster, most often children, and in the depths of torment that can turn towards infantilizing or objectifying or possessing that person. On the flip side separation from their charges induces obsession and depression, punctuated by rage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Disquiet - Unhealth</span></b><br /> <br /> Sooner or later people will become concerned about the safety of the toy. It will be seen as mentally unhealthy, infectious, or unsafe. When the Skin Horse manifests as a person rather than a toy, that person will be an unhealthy influence, or possibly as a poor soul that needs help, preferably help that comes far away from here. Whatever the case, they are not safe to keep around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Wasteland - Askew</span></b><br /> <br /> The Skin Horse wasteland reinforces their Disquiet. It spreads malaise, and while it doesn\u2019t actually give people mental conditions it does play with lighting and sound to make senses unreliable in a way that puts people off balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\">Potential Bestowments</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1f3864\"><i>A Child\u2019s Plaything</i></span></b><br /> <br /> The Skin Horse can appear to be a completely normal child\u2019s toy.<br /> </span><br /> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Skin Horses have some overlap conceptually with the imaginary friend sort of dream-born Promethean? Granted, the concept itself is distinct enough given how they're based more on toys and cherished objects than wholly imaginary entities. One thing I do wonder about is what exactly one created through the traditional route of dead flesh would look like. For obvious reasons they seem to be a Construct-heavy Lineage (perhaps the usual way of things could be inverted, with Constructs being more common among them than &quot;normal&quot; Prometheans? In any case, I like the idea and I would be interested to see it developed further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T15:16:38-07:00","id":1551598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551596#post1551596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you treat them as a strictly scientifically grown workforce then, no they don't fit, but that's not the idea. The Neosapiens are an inspiration for their themes and role in their story, not because they map to promethean alchemy. The GELF are supposed to be what would happen if a Demiurge tried to make something like that, but ended up with a Promethean instead. Like the other lineages they take their inspiration and reinterpret it through the lens of Pyros. If that is reasonable for robots and clones, it is reasonable for genetically engineered life forms.<br /> <br /> If it helps, I actually imagine that for the GELF, the process of growing from biomass is less devouring and growing new flesh and more breaking the original flesh down to cells and rebuilding a body from those cells. That seems the right fit for me. The Neos may be the big inspiration for their torment, disquiet, and the rest, but their &quot;biology&quot; has more to do with Parasite Eve.<br /> <br /> For the ULF, there is no assumption about how they are made, and while three of the four inspirations are lab grown, one of them is literally fused together from various monstrous parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clearer: the Created are consistently animated by a force that overrides the fact that their construction should not allow them to be alive in the conventional sense. It's the &quot;LF&quot; that is the problem, because for all that Prometheans are metaphysically living, they aren't &quot;life forms.&quot; The mitochondrial beings in Parasite Eve are alive without needing the spark of divinity to make them so, but a corpse or a mechanical doll does not live without the Fire.<br /> <br /> The established material for genetically engineered lifeforms in Promethean is that they're clones, whether hybridized or more direct copies of people. Clones aren't a Lineage in Promethean's terms because they aren't Created, just as ghouls aren't a Clan in Requiem \u2014 they're more conventionally alive and the involvement of Azoth in their creation doesn't mess with their essential qualities to the same degree as making an inanimate body capable of getting up and walking around, because using the Divine Fire on living matter is a different fundamental process than that of becoming a genitor/demiurge.<br /> <br /> The existing systems for setting clones on the Pilgrimage are to use their body to make a Promethean like any other instance of the generative act (albeit primed somewhat by the presence of Azoth in their flesh). If you're starting with live biomass that isn't dying as part of the process, what you're making isn't a Promethean but something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T19:21:16-07:00","id":1551609,"title":"","content":"Who said the biomass isn't dying? Who said it was even alive to start with? It's being rendered down and restructured and made to function not because it is viable but because some inner fire is forcing it to keep running.<br /> <br /> If it helps, I can remove the LF from their names since it seems to be a distraction. I didn't think it would be a problem since many of the Lineages were already things brought to &quot;life.&quot; What alternates would you suggest? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T21:00:49-07:00","id":1551612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551609#post1551609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said the biomass isn't dying? Who said it was even alive to start with? It's being rendered down and restructured and made to function not because it is viable but because some inner fire is forcing it to keep running.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're described as being grown rather than constructed, which is rather at odds with the part of the generative act Prometheans attribute to solutio and digestio. You make a Promethean by breaking down the body from its former state in some way before imbuing it with Azoth, and in typical usage &quot;biomass&quot; either refers to living things ecologically or to fuel energetically, neither of which squares particularly well with stuff that is being turned into a shell for a volatile metaphysical substance whose animating process is best likened to Galvanism \u2014 you've consistently described the GELF in terms of their being conventionally alive rather than particularly sophisticated scarecrow-people, and the Divine Fire largely doesn't produce conventionally viable Life as a starting point from the processes used to create a Promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it helps, I can remove the LF from their names since it seems to be a distraction. I didn't think it would be a problem since many of the Lineages were already things brought to &quot;life.&quot; What alternates would you suggest? </div> </div> </div>It's not a nomenclature problem, it's a conceptual problem that happens to be reflected in the name. Genetically engineered lifeforms in fiction don't need an animating humour, nor do they typically have a constitution that renders them uniquely susceptible to fire like many forms of undead being \u2014 their instances of nonviability are typically such that they're better framed in terms of stillbirth, whereas the generative act carried through to completion always results in <i>some</i> type of Created being made.<br /> <br /> Like, to make the comparison very blunt, fictional engineered beings are GMOs and Prometheans are wooden dolls brought to life. No amount of genetic engineering of the trees his wood came from is going to meaningfully make Pinocchio the same type of being as Mewtwo, because the Created are made from stuff that is Not Alive (at best, Dead) given life through a miraculous energy/substance that can also be extracted and used for other purposes that happen to include modifying living beings (which are typically more repeatable than getting lightning to strike twice trying to reliably create Prometheans).<br /> <br /> Setting aside your noted observations that most genetically engineered life in fiction doesn't really gravitate toward a Pilgrimage-analogue (whereas every Promethean past the spiritual infancy covered in their prelude scenes does), it's generally conceivable for them to modify their creation process in a way that allows them to e.g. come out of the tube in an earlier or later stage of development. Meanwhile, with the Created you have either a blank-slate new person with more or less the body that was put together or some number of horrific monsters that body tore itself up into, and in either case the resulting monster doesn't age or consume food with biological digestive processes for reasons that have nothing to do with how robust its telomeres are or how efficient its villi are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T08:35:27-07:00","id":1551624,"title":"","content":"Respectfully, it seems like you are the one trying to force biology into it at this point. If you think that a term (like biomass) has too much baggage to work, suggest another one. Don't take that meaning and try to crowbar it into my mouth when I've already stated that is not my intention.<br /> <br /> I could understand that back at the start because I was light on details in the original descriptions. I'll certainly own that. But at this point you are arguing against something very different from what I'm describing.<br /> <br /> To restate, the GELF and the ULF are only as alive as any other Promethean. Their names are based on the goals of their Demiurges, not the actual results. They were attempts to create life in a specific way (genetic engineering) or for a specific purpose (perfection), but the attempt fell short. They are flavored by their origins the way other lineages are, but like the other lineages they are not a perfect match to their source material. The GELF are not lab grown life, at best they look a bit like it if you squint. They are dead parts assembled into a humanoid body and powered by divine fire, the parts are just much smaller than for other Prometheans.<br /> <br /> So if something seems off with that, ask clarifying questions or make suggestions. It's a lot more helpful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T11:37:10-07:00","id":1551626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551597#post1551597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like Skin Horses have some overlap conceptually with the imaginary friend sort of dream-born Promethean? Granted, the concept itself is distinct enough given how they're based more on toys and cherished objects than wholly imaginary entities. One thing I do wonder about is what exactly one created through the traditional route of dead flesh would look like. For obvious reasons they seem to be a Construct-heavy Lineage (perhaps the usual way of things could be inverted, with Constructs being more common among them than &quot;normal&quot; Prometheans? In any case, I like the idea and I would be interested to see it developed further.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting question. The obvious option is that the fleshed versions are disproportionately made from the remains of children, but that's a mental image I really don't care for. I have fewer problems with the construct versions appearing as children, though.<br /> <br /> In a more general sense, there are two elements that make sense to me. The first is that they have a proportionality problem. Not the mismatched parts issue of the Frankensteins, but an issue that their proportions drift towards caricature. They are supposed to look human, but in a more representative fashion. This is something that is true of the constructed versions too. The second is that even when made from remains, there is still an element of construction to them. Their skin may be tanned to leather, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T15:41:03-07:00","id":1551637,"title":"","content":"I only have 1.5 bits of commentary, both on the Ultimate Life Form.<br /> <br /> 1) Intent usually matters less to the Lineages than method for a reason: the alchemical processes that make the Promethean go are, well, <i>processes</i>. Both the Frankenstein* and Galatean Lineages have progenitors who were out to make perfect entities that lines up nicely with the goal of making ultimate life forms, but what matters to each is what they think that is specifically, and how one can attain it in material and supernatural materials and methods.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind, perhaps you might reapproach the goal less as a Lineage and more modification that can be applied TO the Lineages, possibly as a unique, Legendary Bestowment, or, if you want to try your hand at reviving Athanors-as-Z-Splat, a rare universal Z-Splat Athanor.<br /> <br /> .5) I can't not read this as &quot;Finally, I can play Shadow the Hedgehog in Chronicles!&quot; I know that was not the goal in an way, shape, or form, but I can't stop thinking it.<br /> <br /> *At least until the Frankensteins went from Frankenstein to Mary and Polidori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-12-2025, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T16:52:19-07:00","id":1551642,"title":"","content":"For whatever it's worth, I think the <b>GELF</b> could be renamed to <b>Biomasses</b>, or something similar. Something that leans more on their constitution as a mass of cells, without hinting to it being really alive. Both the Life Form and the Genetically Engineered parts rely heavily on aspects of the source material that you made clear to not be the point.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm unsure if the concept is particularly interesting as a Promethean Lineage rather than Deviants, but I'm not strongly against it. I find the Skin Horses more interesting as potential new Lineages.<br /> <br /> The ULF falls on what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> said: intent is less important than the process. Any Demiurge may be thinking of their creation as the Ultimate Life Form, but how they approach its creation is what really shapes the Lineage. Overall I think this intent is best explored in Deviant simply because it begs for the actual person of the &quot;creator&quot; to be explored in the game, something Deviant does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T19:06:08-07:00","id":1551645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551626#post1551626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an interesting question. The obvious option is that the fleshed versions are disproportionately made from the remains of children, but that's a mental image I really don't care for. I have fewer problems with the construct versions appearing as children, though.<br /> <br /> In a more general sense, there are two elements that make sense to me. The first is that they have a proportionality problem. Not the mismatched parts issue of the Frankensteins, but an issue that their proportions drift towards caricature. They are supposed to look human, but in a more representative fashion. This is something that is true of the constructed versions too. The second is that even when made from remains, there is still an element of construction to them. Their skin may be tanned to leather, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to the first route I think that that's definitely something that the table as a whole would have to talk about; apart from the one example Galateid in the 2e book, the books didn't seem to say much about how commonly the corpses of children were used in generative acts. In any case, the second idea that you had actually reminded me of taxidermy and I think that that is where the Lineage could find it's niche. I think that there is a bit of an overlap with the embalmed appearance of the Osiran Disfigurements, but the whole idea of preserved parts being used to construct some sort of plaything makes it seem distinct enough to me. In that case, Skin Horses would be defined by how their bodies are made up of processed, treated flesh, not in the way that a corpse is treated to preserve it for burial, but in the way that animal hides are treated to become useful goods, like you hinted at with the mention of leather. I think that the aesthetics of mass production and disposability could go a long way in helping to flesh them out. There is some overlap with the themes of Galateids, but one of the main thorough lines of their journey could be struggling to obtain a feeling of worth when they were constructed from cheap yet unsettlingly antiseptic spare parts already removed from their original state in nature. They do not even get a whole corpse that a family could have mourned, just random human body parts, and not even particularly notable ones, as is the case with the Frankenstein. While that does come close to encroaching on Galateid territory, I think that the Lineage that you propose would be distinct in that they were never intended to meet or surpass human perfection at all, which is part of why the Galateid fear that they are nothing but an imitation of humanity is relevant to them. They would be toys, constructed on a whim for trivial ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T07:50:37-07:00","id":1551655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551637#post1551637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only have 1.5 bits of commentary, both on the Ultimate Life Form.<br /> <br /> 1) Intent usually matters less to the Lineages than method for a reason: the alchemical processes that make the Promethean go are, well, <i>processes</i>. Both the Frankenstein* and Galatean Lineages have progenitors who were out to make perfect entities that lines up nicely with the goal of making ultimate life forms, but what matters to each is what they think that is specifically, and how one can attain it in material and supernatural materials and methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. And unique Bestowments and other methods make sense, although they seem to imply a different place in the story. Instead of that arrogance of creation being a legacy, it is closer to a single generational element inflicted by the creator (whether that's a Demiurge or a Promethean), or even an element taken up by the Promethean himself on his journey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> .5) I can't not read this as &quot;Finally, I can play Shadow the Hedgehog in Chronicles!&quot; I know that was not the goal in an way, shape, or form, but I can't stop thinking it. </div> </div> </div>It wasn't, but now that you mention it Shadow fits Promethean better than most of the other inspirations for ULFs. Maybe not in terms of what he is, but he fits better in his history and how he relates to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551642#post1551642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For whatever it's worth, I think the <b>GELF</b> could be renamed to <b>Biomasses</b>, or something similar. Something that leans more on their constitution as a mass of cells, without hinting to it being really alive. Both the Life Form and the Genetically Engineered parts rely heavily on aspects of the source material that you made clear to not be the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly Vat Made? Or just Vats? I'd say Vat Born but I think that's a derogatory term for clones in Mass Effect, so it carries the wrong connotation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other than that, I'm unsure if the concept is particularly interesting as a Promethean Lineage rather than Deviants, but I'm not strongly against it. I find the Skin Horses more interesting as potential new Lineages. </div> </div> </div>In the general sense, I agree. Genetic engineering makes sense as a starting point for a lineage and one that should happen sooner or later because attempting to create new life that way is a very common trope. That said, there's nothing in the origin itself that brings much new to the table (unless, like the Zeka, they break some rules, but that's not the goal here).<br /> <br /> However, I've considered the Neosapiens a good inspiration for Promethean since well before Deviant was published. They do bring a lot to the table such as a different approach to the idea of created servants than I see in either the Tammuz or the Unfleshed, a different approach to Torment, etc. Those resonate well as a Lineage for me.<br /> <br /> Does that have to be paired with genetic engineering? No, it could work with other creation methods, but I don't see a reason to seek out a different origin<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551645#post1551645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In regards to the first route I think that that's definitely something that the table as a whole would have to talk about; apart from the one example Galateid in the 2e book, the books didn't seem to say much about how commonly the corpses of children were used in generative acts. In any case, the second idea that you had actually reminded me of taxidermy and I think that that is where the Lineage could find it's niche. I think that there is a bit of an overlap with the embalmed appearance of the Osiran Disfigurements, but the whole idea of preserved parts being used to construct some sort of plaything makes it seem distinct enough to me. In that case, Skin Horses would be defined by how their bodies are made up of processed, treated flesh, not in the way that a corpse is treated to preserve it for burial, but in the way that animal hides are treated to become useful goods, like you hinted at with the mention of leather. I think that the aesthetics of mass production and disposability could go a long way in helping to flesh them out. There is some overlap with the themes of Galateids, but one of the main thorough lines of their journey could be struggling to obtain a feeling of worth when they were constructed from cheap yet unsettlingly antiseptic spare parts already removed from their original state in nature. They do not even get a whole corpse that a family could have mourned, just random human body parts, and not even particularly notable ones, as is the case with the Frankenstein. While that does come close to encroaching on Galateid territory, I think that the Lineage that you propose would be distinct in that they were never intended to meet or surpass human perfection at all, which is part of why the Galateid fear that they are nothing but an imitation of humanity is relevant to them. They would be toys, constructed on a whim for trivial ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trivial to adults, anyways. I think the connection to children is an important element of the Skin Horses. There's great tension in how the worth of the Skin Horse can vary wildly in the eyes of everyone around him and how his most accessible role models don't have humanity figured out either.<br /> <br /> And I agree, the more I think about it, the more a processed element fits them well. Especially the leather. That's the most intuitive processing method, though incorporating real teeth or ground bones as a stuffing are other ghoulish methods I could see a Promethean coming up with. Can we apply this back to those created through more conventional toy parts?<br /> <br /> Oh, and the original Fuggler dolls, (before Spin Master acquired the rights) were handmade using dental implants so they look like they are made with real human teeth. I did not intend to use them as visual inspiration, but given the construction method we are moving towards, they make a lot of sense. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img alt=\"Mr. Buttons\" title=\"Mr. Buttons\" width=\"200\" height=\"224\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://www.louisemcg.com/uploads/1/3/0/5/130503915/fuggler2_orig.jpg\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://www.louisemcg.com/uploads/1/3/0/5/130503915/fuggler2_orig.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://www.louisemcg.com/uploads/1/3/0/5/130503915/fuggler2_orig.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Mr. Buttons\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div></div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T10:23:51-07:00","id":1551658,"title":"","content":"Vat Made seems good enough, maybe Vat Built. I'd avoid Vat Born, again, because it unnecessarily hints to a biological process, instead of just organic composition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T15:39:27-07:00","id":1551667,"title":"","content":"Way back in the day, I came up with a pair of Lineages to complement the Zeka, a sort of &quot;Hazmat trio&quot;: where the Zeka are personifications of nuclear/radioactive calamities, one of the other Lineages would be chemical/toxic, and the other would be biological/plague golems. Looking back at it, it might be better to view those as precursors to the Nuclear Prometheans, much like Dark Eras gave us the Lineage that Frankensteins replaced; and there's not enough of a difference between them to justify two separate Lineages. But I digress. I mention it to point out that I've got no problem with Lineages where the generative process is biological; vat-born works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T21:06:47-07:00","id":1551670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551655#post1551655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair. And unique Bestowments and other methods make sense, although they seem to imply a different place in the story. Instead of that arrogance of creation being a legacy, it is closer to a single generational element inflicted by the creator (whether that's a Demiurge or a Promethean), or even an element taken up by the Promethean himself on his journey.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It wasn't, but now that you mention it Shadow fits Promethean better than most of the other inspirations for ULFs. Maybe not in terms of what he is, but he fits better in his history and how he relates to others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Possibly Vat Made? Or just Vats? I'd say Vat Born but I think that's a derogatory term for clones in Mass Effect, so it carries the wrong connotation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the general sense, I agree. Genetic engineering makes sense as a starting point for a lineage and one that should happen sooner or later because attempting to create new life that way is a very common trope. That said, there's nothing in the origin itself that brings much new to the table (unless, like the Zeka, they break some rules, but that's not the goal here).<br /> <br /> However, I've considered the Neosapiens a good inspiration for Promethean since well before Deviant was published. They do bring a lot to the table such as a different approach to the idea of created servants than I see in either the Tammuz or the Unfleshed, a different approach to Torment, etc. Those resonate well as a Lineage for me.<br /> <br /> Does that have to be paired with genetic engineering? No, it could work with other creation methods, but I don't see a reason to seek out a different origin<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Trivial to adults, anyways. I think the connection to children is an important element of the Skin Horses. There's great tension in how the worth of the Skin Horse can vary wildly in the eyes of everyone around him and how his most accessible role models don't have humanity figured out either.<br /> <br /> And I agree, the more I think about it, the more a processed element fits them well. Especially the leather. That's the most intuitive processing method, though incorporating real teeth or ground bones as a stuffing are other ghoulish methods I could see a Promethean coming up with. Can we apply this back to those created through more conventional toy parts?<br /> <br /> Oh, and the original Fuggler dolls, (before Spin Master acquired the rights) were handmade using dental implants so they look like they are made with real human teeth. I did not intend to use them as visual inspiration, but given the construction method we are moving towards, they make a lot of sense.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img alt=\"Mr. Buttons\" title=\"Mr. Buttons\" width=\"200\" height=\"224\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://www.louisemcg.com/uploads/1/3/0/5/130503915/fuggler2_orig.jpg\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://www.louisemcg.com/uploads/1/3/0/5/130503915/fuggler2_orig.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://www.louisemcg.com/uploads/1/3/0/5/130503915/fuggler2_orig.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Mr. Buttons\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it does seem like &quot;overlooked value&quot; is the operative theme with them, perhaps even being disregarded by other Prometheans until they can display some insight that those primarily emulating adults cannot grasp. I think you're right in that their approach to the Pilgrimage is going to be pretty heavily defined by their relationship with children, which is probably where a lot of Skin Horses diverge. On one hand, trying to find a kid to emulate in order to attain humanity seems pretty obvious based on their nature, but one can see some growing resentful at those they were made for, given how they got a free ride to mortality while they have to struggle for the New Dawn. And if they go with the companion toy route, if their chosen role model is affected by their Disquiet I can see them becoming obsessive in trying to win the child's affections back, whether that involve keeping them from mortal friends, trying to force situations in which they can be useful again, and such. I can actually see them working a bit like Galateids when it comes to the desire to have a mortal companion on the Pilgrimage even when they know it will probably end in tragedy, just with juveniles.<br /> <br /> Interestingly enough, given how the toy form thing was supposed to be a Bestowment, presumably they might not actually appear to the mortal objects of their affections with their normal body? Just thinking in terms of normal gameplay and having to walk around and do stuff with the party. It might promote some sort of double life thing, or they might just try to pass off as a normal human, I suppose. As for the idea of incorporating actual body parts in their construction that definitely sounds good, works with the base Promethean nature and adds in some of that horror kid's show aesthetic (Had not seen a Fuggler doll before. It looks disturbing, in the good way.). Think that their hair could definitely just be cut animal or human hair, as is used in some wigs. <br /> <br /> Also, maybe Vat Grown could work for the GELFs? Carries a more organic connotation than Vat Made, while still keeping the artificial connotation that Vat Born has less of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T08:54:17-07:00","id":1551721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551667#post1551667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Way back in the day, I came up with a pair of Lineages to complement the Zeka, a sort of &quot;Hazmat trio&quot;: where the Zeka are personifications of nuclear/radioactive calamities, one of the other Lineages would be chemical/toxic, and the other would be biological/plague golems. Looking back at it, it might be better to view those as precursors to the Nuclear Prometheans, much like Dark Eras gave us the Lineage that Frankensteins replaced; and there's not enough of a difference between them to justify two separate Lineages. But I digress. I mention it to point out that I've got no problem with Lineages where the generative process is biological; vat-born works for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vat Born does flows the best, verbally, though I think Vat Grown is a close second and has the advantage of being slightly akilter.<br /> <br /> The idea of biological themes for Prometheans doesn't bother me, either. I don't mean that I would expect a promethean to have a biology that functions exactly like a human, but I can easily see that divine fire operating through a biological lens.<br /> <br /> Parasite Eve is a very good template for this, actually. The neo mitochondrial creatures look biological, but it is an impossible biology driven by an outside force (the rebel mitochondria). This is most obvious with the Central Park Flesh Mass, but it is apparent in many of the others too. The cells may or may not be alive, but if they are they are alive despite the fact that they can't actually exist that way. I don't see a reason that the Azoth couldn't do something similar and force a functionality that shouldn't be possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551670#post1551670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it does seem like &quot;overlooked value&quot; is the operative theme with them, perhaps even being disregarded by other Prometheans until they can display some insight that those primarily emulating adults cannot grasp. I think you're right in that their approach to the Pilgrimage is going to be pretty heavily defined by their relationship with children, which is probably where a lot of Skin Horses diverge. On one hand, trying to find a kid to emulate in order to attain humanity seems pretty obvious based on their nature, but one can see some growing resentful at those they were made for, given how they got a free ride to mortality while they have to struggle for the New Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of my favorite elements of the lineage, that children underscore something important. They don't have humanity figured out either, but they are still human and the Skin Horses aren't. Children bring forward a primal fear to Skin Horses, that seeking to understand humanity may be the completely wrong path but it is still the only path they can see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if they go with the companion toy route, if their chosen role model is affected by their Disquiet I can see them becoming obsessive in trying to win the child's affections back, whether that involve keeping them from mortal friends, trying to force situations in which they can be useful again, and such. I can actually see them working a bit like Galateids when it comes to the desire to have a mortal companion on the Pilgrimage even when they know it will probably end in tragedy, just with juveniles. </div> </div> </div>I can see several ways that Disquiet might affect their chosen person, and I'm not sure which one is best. Perhaps any of them could happen.<br /> <br /> First there is the Toy Story route, where the chosen abandons the Promethean. As this is disquiet, it is a little more profound than a child just growing up. It may manifest as outgrowing the toy but more severe, a brutal cold shoulder or a revulsion rather than mere forgetting. This style of Disquiet plays well into the Skin Horse's torment.<br /> <br /> Then there is the quiet dependency. The child doesn't change much, but they take the promethean everywhere and become deeply distressed if separated. Given long enough, separation becomes physically dangerous. This version plays into the general Disquiet that everyone but the chosen experiences.<br /> <br /> The third way is a deep and troublesome obsession with the toy. Being around it changes the chosen one's behavior in unhealthy ways. If the promethean actually communicates with him, the child will misunderstand in dangerous ways. If the promethean doesn't, the child will still feel it is urging him to do things anyways. Note that here the obsession is not with the promethean, per se, but with a false understanding of him. This version plays into the misplaced value theme.<br /> <br /> Two things of note about these.<br /> <br /> 1) They work even if the Promethean doesn't use his bestowment. I wrote them as if he did, but the chosen one can manifest these same behaviors towards a person as towards a toy. The Bestowment facilitates the Skin Horse storyline, but it shouldn't define it.<br /> <br /> 2) They work whether or not the chosen one is a child. While I do think the Lineage should be connected to children, almost certainly there will come a point in a Skin Horse's pilgrimage where they try to step outside that. So it is important that their challenges work regardless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interestingly enough, given how the toy form thing was supposed to be a Bestowment, presumably they might not actually appear to the mortal objects of their affections with their normal body? Just thinking in terms of normal gameplay and having to walk around and do stuff with the party. It might promote some sort of double life thing, or they might just try to pass off as a normal human, I suppose. </div> </div> </div>It is quite possible. Another question I have is how often Skin Horses appear to be children. I mentioned before I think it is fitting for them to often have a childlike normal form. I wouldn't lock them into that, but perhaps adult appearing Skin Horses are the exception, not the rule.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T16:44:55-07:00","id":1551728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551721#post1551721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vat Born does flows the best, verbally, though I think Vat Grown is a close second and has the advantage of being slightly akilter.<br /> <br /> The idea of biological themes for Prometheans doesn't bother me, either. I don't mean that I would expect a promethean to have a biology that functions exactly like a human, but I can easily see that divine fire operating through a biological lens.<br /> <br /> Parasite Eve is a very good template for this, actually. The neo mitochondrial creatures look biological, but it is an impossible biology driven by an outside force (the rebel mitochondria). This is most obvious with the Central Park Flesh Mass, but it is apparent in many of the others too. The cells may or may not be alive, but if they are they are alive despite the fact that they can't actually exist that way. I don't see a reason that the Azoth couldn't do something similar and force a functionality that shouldn't be possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is one of my favorite elements of the lineage, that children underscore something important. They don't have humanity figured out either, but they are still human and the Skin Horses aren't. Children bring forward a primal fear to Skin Horses, that seeking to understand humanity may be the completely wrong path but it is still the only path they can see.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I can see several ways that Disquiet might affect their chosen person, and I'm not sure which one is best. Perhaps any of them could happen.<br /> <br /> First there is the Toy Story route, where the chosen abandons the Promethean. As this is disquiet, it is a little more profound than a child just growing up. It may manifest as outgrowing the toy but more severe, a brutal cold shoulder or a revulsion rather than mere forgetting. This style of Disquiet plays well into the Skin Horse's torment.<br /> <br /> Then there is the quiet dependency. The child doesn't change much, but they take the promethean everywhere and become deeply distressed if separated. Given long enough, separation becomes physically dangerous. This version plays into the general Disquiet that everyone but the chosen experiences.<br /> <br /> The third way is a deep and troublesome obsession with the toy. Being around it changes the chosen one's behavior in unhealthy ways. If the promethean actually communicates with him, the child will misunderstand in dangerous ways. If the promethean doesn't, the child will still feel it is urging him to do things anyways. Note that here the obsession is not with the promethean, per se, but with a false understanding of him. This version plays into the misplaced value theme.<br /> <br /> Two things of note about these.<br /> <br /> 1) They work even if the Promethean doesn't use his bestowment. I wrote them as if he did, but the chosen one can manifest these same behaviors towards a person as towards a toy. The Bestowment facilitates the Skin Horse storyline, but it shouldn't define it.<br /> <br /> 2) They work whether or not the chosen one is a child. While I do think the Lineage should be connected to children, almost certainly there will come a point in a Skin Horse's pilgrimage where they try to step outside that. So it is important that their challenges work regardless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It is quite possible. Another question I have is how often Skin Horses appear to be children. I mentioned before I think it is fitting for them to often have a childlike normal form. I wouldn't lock them into that, but perhaps adult appearing Skin Horses are the exception, not the rule.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The points that you shared sound good; I particularly liked the mention of how they Lineage grasps the theme of questioning the value of the human condition but choosing it anyway. While I usually think of religious and mystical Lineages when it comes to that, in keeping with historical skepticism of humanity (as is seen to a degree with the Osirans and the Ulgans), the way you described it actually sounds pretty convincing. Specifically, the sort of framing that it implies suggests that something of the &quot;default route&quot; for that sort of Promethean would be maintaining a simple faith in the promise of mortality, which ties them back to the children they are associated with. As for the Disquiets, I like the third one that you mentioned, I think it leads to more tension and tragedy when there is less outright revulsion and more of an unhealthy relationship, in that case, literally objectifying the Promethean by focusing upon the image that they have of them in their mind rather than the actual person. As for the last point, I think that that sounds like a good idea. Basically having the opposite sort of demographic spread compared to the average Prometheans, who are pretty heavily implied to usually appear like adults. That also has the bonus of leaving open possibilities for different sorts of Pilgrimages, in regards to what they do after and however they internalized the trials they faced on the way.<br /> <br /> I think that Vat Born for GELFs might be okay in and of itself? I think the main advantage is that it has a certain familiarity to it for most people that has been provided by popular culture. Also, having the natural sounding &quot;born&quot; with the distinctly artificial sounding &quot;vat&quot; has a nice dissonance. Other than that, it is difficult to really come up with good titles that are concise and atmospheric. I thought of something like Vat Cultured, but it does not have much of a ring to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T20:53:52-07:00","id":1551731,"title":"","content":"The problem with Vat Born is what Satchel was explaining earlier: Prometheans are necessarily not born. They have no metabolism, no biological process, even if made out of biomass. They've never been alive except by fiat from the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> Calling them &quot;born&quot; gives the impression of a living process that didn't really exist (otherwise they wouldn't be Prometheans, they would be Deviants). They're made from a mass of cells grown in a vat, that's true, but this mass doesn't form an organism. They're either dead or, if living, unable to really live on as a whole organism. <b>As far as creating a living organism is concerned, they are a <u>failure</u></b>.<br /> <br /> Now, while a name is &quot;just&quot; a name, we've already seen in this very topic how much it can cause misunderstandings, and here it may cause a wrong impression about the actual themes of the Lineage.<br /> <br /> Other than that, while Vat has an artificial connotation, it already has a strong theme of biomass. Vat Grown I think to be a very good option, referring to the way the biomass was obtained rather than the &quot;organism&quot; itself.<br /> <br /> Another idea I just had is to name them <b>Roboti</b>, the original word used in the play <i>R.U.R.</i>, as I think the roboti from the play are specially good examples of the themes of the Lineage and it would bypass the matter entirely (despite bringing certain confusion with the later meaning of the word <i>robot</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T07:57:17-07:00","id":1551735,"title":"","content":"Czech may be the right approach. What about The Pestovani? It's a Czech word for cultivated but with an mismatching Latinized plural. It's probably not the most applicable Czech word, but the other one I found was Kultivovana, which is too much like the English word.<br /> <br /> Of course, I don't know any Czech so all of that was developed through Google Translate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T12:11:34-07:00","id":1551741,"title":"","content":"Pestovani seems good. For whatever it's worth, Roboti is a made-up word (the actual word is Robot<u><b>a</b></u>), but that's not here or there.<br /> <br /> For whatever it's worth, my point was to keep with the theme of naming lineages after legendary/classic members. Osiris, Tamuz and \u00dclgen are gods, Amirani and Galatea are mythic &quot;heroes&quot;, and Frankenstein is a book. Maybe they could also be called Rossum (from <i>R.U.R.</i>)? But Pestovani has a roll in the tongue that I like, and Zeka is already a Russian word, so using Czech isn't out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-26T14:14:41-07:00","id":1551875,"title":"","content":"Some of my thoughts for the Pestovani:<br /> <br /> In stories of genetically engineered servants there is a frequent focus on the conflict between what they were created to do and their fundamental worth as a human or human-adjacent. That's certainly the case with some of the inspirations for the Pestovani. I think a good way of exploring this <br /> <br /> The Pestovani are a created servant lineage, like the Tammuz and Unfleshed, but their relationship to the role is quite different. They are servants by intent, not by nature. Indeed there's nothing in their Humour or Torment that makes them particularly servile or adapted to labor. Instead this element is expressed entirely through their Disquiet. People unnaturally compartmentalize the Pestovani into narrow, rigid, and devalued roles. Frequently these are negative stereotypes that justify dehumanizing attitudes of suspicion or exploitation, but even when they are positive or neutral stereotypes they are still devaluing roles like &quot;one of the few good ones&quot; or a &quot;token friend,&quot; or &quot;the help.&quot; Breaking free of these roles, even by something as minor as having the wrong opinion, will shock and frighten those in the grip of Disquiet and the Promethean will rapidly be recompartmentalized into a darker, less trusted role. And because the roles are so narrow and the rules of them frequently unstated it is difficult for a Pestovani to stay within them even if he wants to.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly the Pestovani have picked up a reputation for rebellion, although this too has nothing to do with their nature.<br /> <br /> While their Torment does not have anything to do with this theme directly, it is designed to play badly with their Disquiet. It makes it more difficult for them to play along with inflicted roles even if they want to, It's also an important reminder of their promethean nature, which is important because I think they need reminding of that.<br /> <br /> Tell me if this part makes sense:<br /> <br /> Because the Disquiet so often devalues them, quite a few Pestovani take the attitude that even if they are not human yet, they at least have (or at least should have) all the same worth and dignity. Now that's a good lesson if it is a hard earned step on the Pilgrimage, but it can be skipping quite a few steps for younger Prometheans who don't have a grasp on what dignity and worth even mean. This is not an attitude inherent to the lineage, just one that the circumstances they often find themselves in bring about.<br /> <br /> I also think that there is a small but notable minority (which with Promethean numbers, might mean two actual Pestovani) who are seeking to gain humanity but not to become humans. These few reason that humanity is just a quality humans have, not one restricted to them. They still seek to complete the Great Work they just don't intend to be quite human at the end of it. If any of them have achieved this, no living Promethean has heard about it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I have this idea that their demiurge died in the process of creating the first one. Basically he was working with only animal cells, but he fell in the vat during the final experiment and his body became the mass for the first of the Pestovani. As for when this happened, I could see these experiments happening any time from the mid 1800s on.<br /> <br /> This raises the possibility that Pestovani may be made at least partially from other species so long as at least some human mass is involved. It may be quite common for them to have animalistic features for disfigurements. Other possible disfigurements include unnatural growths and strange bone structure.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T21:09:08-07:00","id":1551892,"title":"","content":"The attitude makes sense. It is a recurring theme in all Lineages that they tend to have a certain revulsion against the expectations linked to their &quot;nature&quot;. Unfleshed and Tammuz are especially prone to revolt against being treated as slaves/tools. As someone frequently dehumanized, it makes sense for the Pestovani to be quick and firm to form a notion of self worth.<br /> <br /> About not wanting to become human <i>per se</i>, I think this is something kind of missing in Promethean in general, but ultimately it is complicated. I think it's a valuable notion to add to the game, but not necessarily restricted to a particular Lineage. Anyway, this is at least partially covered by the rules on going throw the New Dawn choosing to retain your memories.<br /> <br /> On the Demiurge, it's good to remember that since 2nd Edition a Lineage doesn't have a single Demiurge anymore: there's an original one, but the process is repeatable by other humans. But I think this story is a good one. Not many Lineages are conducive of the Demiurge becoming a part of the Created, especially so directly (I can think Ulgan, Faceless and Zeka undergoing something similar in some way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T07:20:46-07:00","id":1551941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1551559-lineage-ideas?p=1551892#post1551892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The attitude makes sense. It is a recurring theme in all Lineages that they tend to have a certain revulsion against the expectations linked to their &quot;nature&quot;. Unfleshed and Tammuz are especially prone to revolt against being treated as slaves/tools. As someone frequently dehumanized, it makes sense for the Pestovani to be quick and firm to form a notion of self worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping so. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About not wanting to become human <i>per se</i>, I think this is something kind of missing in Promethean in general, but ultimately it is complicated. I think it's a valuable notion to add to the game, but not necessarily restricted to a particular Lineage. Anyway, this is at least partially covered by the rules on going throw the New Dawn choosing to retain your memories. </div> </div> </div>I agree, like many of the things I associate with the Pestovani, this motivation wouldn't be unique to the lineage, though it might be more common within it. I also think it is important that Prometheans should not know if this is viable or not. It may be, but it also may be a hindrance to the Pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the Demiurge, it's good to remember that since 2nd Edition a Lineage doesn't have a single Demiurge anymore: there's an original one, but the process is repeatable by other humans. But I think this story is a good one. Not many Lineages are conducive of the Demiurge becoming a part of the Created, especially so directly (I can think Ulgan, Faceless and Zeka undergoing something similar in some way). </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Originally, I was going to suggest that the first was created that way and the next several Pestovani were created by the original Demiurge's business partners. That was largely to give them a small boost in initial numbers and a common initial experience as created servants. I realized, though, that the Pestovani would also work well with experiments with pre- and counter-mendelian genetic theories (such as pangenesis and Lysenkoism, though the Demiurge would be using some strange variant) so the Lineage could reasonably be older than I first envisioned.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea that the first was intended to be created without human remains, though. It resonates quite well thematically if they were intended to be non-human and they aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T10:44:31-07:00","id":1551946,"title":"","content":"I think it is a sound concept for their Progenitor. Human <i>form</i> is more important to a Promethean than human <i>tissue</i>, and even this form can be as abstract as a chatbot, so this isn't something too distinct from what we already see in the corebook alone. A Progenitor that isn't meant to be human in anything but surface appearance is a welcome novelty. And it feeds again in the notion that however &quot;biological&quot; their creation seems, it's ultimately the same alchemy of every Promethean, animating a nonsensical basis through the <i>idea</i> of a human and the Divine Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T14:42:19-07:00","id":1553612,"title":"","content":"I realized yesterday that there's a wonderful resonance between the creation method of Skin Horses and the idea behind them. At first glance it doesn't seem that way. They are supposed to be the creations of children, or at least that's their most common demiurge. Processing human remains is outside the reach of most children (thankfully).<br /> <br /> Except...<br /> <br /> There is one appropriate thing children can get their hands on more easily than adults... teeth. Specifically their own baby teeth. The ghoulish example of dolls made with human teeth is likely more common than I originally thought, and more innocent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-03T19:17:21-07:00","id":1553617,"title":"","content":"Parents and caretakers are more likely to keep those baby teeth than the children themselves. They're also the more probable source of dolls, even dolls with actual human teeth (that do not need to be baby teeth). Humans have traded a lot on teeth until quite recently, and it isn't something that simply went away even IRL.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that the idea of the body not being made by the Demiurge themselves may be a peculiarity of the Skin Horses we can lean on. Maybe a part of the Alchemy that makes them begins in the love an adult puts in the toy, either towards the child or towards the toy itself, and sits waiting for the child to complete the Work.<br /> <br /> But I would still twist the story of the Velveteen Rabbit a bit to better fit this Creation. Maybe the love isn't really all it takes. The child usually haven't made the body of the doll, because they can't, but they did do <i>something</i>. Some form of ritual, one that fits a child and their desperation for companionship, gives the last quick of Alchemy. Maybe the child will later forget what they did, maybe never. Maybe it is so instinctual that Skin Horses may have been the very first Lineage, or maybe among the many stories and plays children share, there's a ritual being passed down for untold years that can be performed as just them playing with the toy, but that calls on the Divine Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T11:40:41-07:00","id":1553711,"title":"","content":"I do prefer the idea that whatever calls down the Divine Fire, it is the work of the child not dependent on a specific, unintentional contribution from an adult. If that means that the kind of vessel that works for a demiurge and the kind of vessel that works for a Promethean are different, I am okay with that. <br /> <br /> I really like the idea that Skin Horses have been around a long, long time and that this is something that keeps happening. The name would be a much more recent addition (or be an old name that somehow found its name into a book). I suspect, though, that if the lineage has been around that long it hasn't been so continuously. That is, that children have recreated it multiple times over the millenia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T07:10:30-07:00","id":1562300,"title":"","content":"So here\u2019s a \u2018fun\u2019 potential interaction for the Skin Horses. It\u2019s a child\u2019s popup book I recently saw. The book is flimsy in both physical structure and story. Four sock puppet animals are looking for their babies, the reader can find them by lifting the flaps. We don\u2019t dwell on the worry of the parents because we can resolve it so quickly. In fact, we never really see how the parents respond to what they are seeing. It\u2019s simply setup for the popup surprise. Then there\u2019s one last page where all four babies get to pop out of the book one last time. Hooray!<br /> <br /> Except\u2026 the book takes damage rather easily especially to the popup pieces. So now instead of finding the baby animals safe and sound, they are damaged and torn. In one case, mama sloth finds her child with its head missing. In a dark coincidence, that same baby sloth has fallen entirely out of the final popup adding to the grimness of its first reveal.<br /> <br /> Now, there\u2019s nothing actually horrible here. It\u2019s just regular wear and tear on a child\u2019s book. In fact, I know how the book was damaged and it was purely accidental. But what does a young Promethean think when they pick up this text? What do they think when the parents tape the book back together?<br /> <br /> At the very least it sounds like potential inspiration for a milestone and since it connect well to the Skin Horses, I figured I\u2019d put it here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}